E('great zimbabwe', 'Great Zimbabwe is a ruined medieval city in south-east Africa.', 'It flourished from about the 11th to the 15th century.', 'Its huge stone walls were built without mortar.', 'It was the capital of a wealthy trading kingdom.', 'It traded gold and ivory as far as China.', 'The modern country of Zimbabwe is named after it.')
E('kingdom of kush|kush|nubia', 'The Kingdom of Kush was an ancient African kingdom in Nubia, south of Egypt.', 'It lasted from around 1070 BC to AD 350.', 'Kushite kings ruled Egypt as its 25th Dynasty.', 'Its capital later moved to Meroë.', 'Sudan has more pyramids than Egypt, built by the Kushites.')
E('aksum|axum', 'Aksum was a powerful ancient kingdom in what is now Ethiopia and Eritrea.', 'It flourished from about the 1st to the 7th century AD.', 'It traded with Rome, Persia and India.', 'It minted its own coins.', 'It adopted Christianity in the 4th century.', 'Its giant stone obelisks still stand.')
E('ethiopia', 'Ethiopia is a country in the Horn of Africa, one of the oldest nations in the world.', 'It traces its history back thousands of years.', 'Its capital is Addis Ababa.', 'It was never colonised, apart from an Italian occupation from 1936 to 1941.', 'It defeated Italy at the Battle of Adwa in 1896.', 'Coffee is thought to originate there.')
E('scramble for africa', 'The Scramble for Africa was the rapid colonisation of Africa by European powers.', 'It happened mostly between 1881 and 1914.', 'The Berlin Conference of 1884 to 1885 set rules for claiming land.', 'By 1914, only Ethiopia and Liberia were independent.', 'Borders were drawn with little regard for local peoples.', 'Most African countries won independence in the 1950s and 1960s.')
E('shaka zulu|zulu', 'Shaka was the founder of the Zulu Kingdom in southern Africa.', 'He lived from about 1787 to 1828.', 'He reorganised the Zulu army with new tactics.', 'He introduced a short stabbing spear.', 'He built a powerful kingdom.', 'The Zulu later defeated the British at Isandlwana in 1879.')
E('mughal empire|mughals|akbar', 'The Mughal Empire ruled most of the Indian subcontinent.', 'It lasted from 1526 to 1857.', 'It was founded by Babur, a descendant of Genghis Khan.', 'Akbar the Great was famed for religious tolerance.', 'Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal.', 'It declined as British power grew.')
E('khmer empire', 'The Khmer Empire was a powerful state in South-East Asia.', 'It lasted from 802 to 1431.', 'Its capital was Angkor, in Cambodia.', 'It built Angkor Wat.', 'It had sophisticated water management systems.')
E('tang dynasty', 'The Tang dynasty is often seen as a golden age of Chinese civilisation.', 'It ruled from 618 to 907.', 'Its capital, Chang’an, was one of the largest cities in the world.', 'Poetry flourished, with poets like Li Bai and Du Fu.', 'Woodblock printing developed.', 'Wu Zetian, China’s only female emperor, ruled during this period.')
E('ming dynasty|forbidden city', 'The Ming dynasty ruled China, and built the Forbidden City in Beijing.', 'It ruled from 1368 to 1644.', 'The Forbidden City was completed in 1420.', 'It has hundreds of buildings.', 'Ming porcelain is world-famous.', 'Much of the Great Wall seen today was built under the Ming.')
E('qing dynasty|last emperor|puyi', 'The Qing was China’s last imperial dynasty.', 'It ruled from 1644 to 1912.', 'It was founded by the Manchus.', 'It lost wars to Britain, France and Japan.', 'The last emperor, Puyi, abdicated in 1912 at age six.', 'China then became a republic.')
E('sun yat-sen', 'Sun Yat-sen was a Chinese revolutionary and the first president of the Republic of China.', 'He lived from 1866 to 1925.', 'He led the movement that overthrew the Qing dynasty.', 'He is called the “Father of the Nation” in Taiwan.', 'He is honoured in mainland China too.')
E('tiananmen square|tiananmen', 'Tiananmen Square is a large public square in Beijing.', 'In 1989 it was the centre of pro-democracy protests.', 'Students and workers gathered there for weeks.', 'The government declared martial law.', 'On 3 and 4 June 1989 the army cleared the protests, killing many people.', 'The image of “Tank Man” became world-famous.')
E('american revolution heroes|paul revere', 'Paul Revere was an American silversmith and patriot.', 'He lived from 1735 to 1818.', 'On 18 April 1775 he rode to warn that British troops were coming.', 'He did not actually shout “The British are coming!”', 'A poem by Longfellow made his ride famous.')
E('louisiana purchase', 'The Louisiana Purchase was the United States’ purchase of a vast territory from France.', 'It was made in 1803.', 'It doubled the size of the US.', 'The price was $15 million, about four cents an acre.', 'Napoleon sold it to fund his wars.')
E('trail of tears', 'The Trail of Tears was the forced removal of Native American nations from their lands in the south-eastern US.', 'It took place mainly between 1830 and 1850.', 'It followed the Indian Removal Act of 1830.', 'The Cherokee, Muscogee, Seminole, Chickasaw and Choctaw were forced west.', 'Thousands died from cold, disease and hunger.')
E('native americans|first nations|indigenous americans', 'Native Americans are the Indigenous peoples of the Americas.', 'Their ancestors arrived at least 15,000 years ago.', 'Hundreds of distinct nations developed, with many languages.', 'European diseases killed a large share after 1492.', 'Wars and forced removals took much of their land.', 'Many nations keep their cultures and governments today.')
E('sitting bull|little bighorn|crazy horse', 'Sitting Bull was a Hunkpapa Lakota leader.', 'He lived from about 1831 to 1890.', 'He led resistance to US government policies.', 'Lakota and Cheyenne warriors defeated Custer at the Little Bighorn in 1876.', 'Crazy Horse was a leading war chief there.', 'Sitting Bull was killed by police in 1890.')
E('mexican revolution|pancho villa|emiliano zapata', 'The Mexican Revolution was a long armed struggle in Mexico.', 'It lasted from 1910 to about 1920.', 'It began against the dictator Porfirio Díaz.', 'Leaders included Pancho Villa and Emiliano Zapata.', 'Zapata fought for land for poor farmers.', 'It led to the constitution of 1917.')
E('canada history|confederation', 'Canada became a self-governing country through Confederation.', 'Confederation happened on 1 July 1867, now Canada Day.', 'It began with four provinces.', 'Sir John A. Macdonald was its first prime minister.', 'It gained full legal independence in 1982.')
E('australian history|first fleet', 'Modern Australian history began with British colonisation.', 'The First Fleet arrived at Sydney Cove on 26 January 1788.', 'It carried convicts and marines.', 'About 160,000 convicts were sent to Australia.', 'The colonies federated in 1901.', 'Aboriginal peoples suffered dispossession and violence.')
E('new zealand|aotearoa|treaty of waitangi', 'New Zealand is an island country in the South Pacific.', 'Māori settled it around 1300.', 'Its Māori name is Aotearoa.', 'The Treaty of Waitangi was signed in 1840.', 'It was the first country to give women the vote, in 1893.', 'Its capital is Wellington.')
E('wars of the roses', 'The Wars of the Roses were English civil wars between the houses of Lancaster and York.', 'They lasted from 1455 to 1487.', 'The red rose stood for Lancaster, the white for York.', 'Richard III was killed at Bosworth in 1485.', 'Henry VII founded the Tudor dynasty.', 'Richard III’s skeleton was found under a car park in 2012.')
E('tudors|tudor', 'The Tudors were a royal dynasty that ruled England.', 'They ruled from 1485 to 1603.', 'They began with Henry VII.', 'Henry VIII broke with the Catholic Church.', 'Elizabeth I was the last Tudor.', 'Their era saw the English Reformation and Renaissance.')
E('scotland', 'Scotland is a country that is part of the United Kingdom.', 'It united with England in 1707.', 'Its capital is Edinburgh.', 'It has its own legal system and parliament.', 'It voted to stay in the UK in a 2014 referendum.', 'Its inventors gave the world the telephone, TV and penicillin.')
E('wales', 'Wales is a country that is part of the United Kingdom.', 'It was conquered by England in the 13th century.', 'Its capital is Cardiff.', 'Welsh is one of Europe’s oldest living languages.', 'It has its own parliament, the Senedd.')
E('northern ireland|the troubles', 'Northern Ireland is part of the United Kingdom, and the Troubles were a conflict there.', 'The Troubles lasted from the late 1960s to 1998.', 'It was a conflict between mainly Catholic nationalists and mainly Protestant unionists.', 'About 3,500 people were killed.', 'The Good Friday Agreement of 1998 largely ended it.')
E('french resistance', 'The French Resistance fought Nazi occupation in France.', 'It was active from 1940 to 1944.', 'Members sabotaged railways and gathered intelligence.', 'Many were women.', 'They helped the Allies during D-Day.')
E('marshall plan', 'The Marshall Plan was an American program to rebuild Western Europe after the Second World War.', 'It ran from 1948 to 1952.', 'The US gave over $13 billion.', 'It was named after Secretary of State George Marshall.', 'It helped Europe recover quickly.')
